{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641943,"nonce":"0O7PHuGxrDv7WFp5ZwgDpOzKBV0=","title":"Interpreter dispatch does a hash probe per instruction and hashes the symbol pool per frame","message":"hir_interp.rs run_frame: while pc \u003c code.len() does self.profile.get_mut(\u0026func_id) for every executed instruction. Each frame also builds resolved_symbols by hashing every name in the function's symbol pool (up to two string-keyed lookups each), and allocates regs, visits, slots, deferred, wanted and an args Vec before running.\n\nA function with a 20-symbol pool hashes 20 strings on every call whether or not it reaches them. Both lengthen the interpreter-served first iteration.\n\nDirection: count in a local and flush at frame exit; resolve symbols lazily or once per CompiledFunction. See also the register-stack and untagged-register ideas on the interpreter.","files":null}]}